drum2midi-gui: build recipe only

This repository contains a build recipe. It contains no model weights, no upstream
code (only a submodule pointer) and no built application. The licence in LICENSE
covers the recipe alone.

Everything below is fetched at build time onto the builder's own machine.
Its licences are its own; sha256 values are enforced from recipe/checksums.txt.

  drum2midi (submodule upstream/)   https://github.com/miraer/drum2midi @ ef2a36c062341ab0ea585874259ea396a94ae362
  ADTOF-pytorch                     https://github.com/xavriley/ADTOF-pytorch @ 85c192e78f716ea0b111cc8a5ee4a8f6a3a4f8a9
                                    (no licence file; ADTOF weights are CC BY-NC-SA 4.0)
  MDX23C separator checkpoint       fetched by audio-separator (licence per its model card)
  htdemucs                          fetched by audio-separator (MIT, Meta)
  MuseScore_General.sf3             https://ftp.osuosl.org/pub/musescore/soundfont/MuseScore_General/MuseScore_General.sf3
  ffmpeg (static arm64)             imageio-ffmpeg wheel (GPL/LGPL build of FFmpeg)
  fluidsynth + dylibs               Homebrew fluid-synth (LGPL 2.1+) relocated with dylibbundler
  PySide6 / Qt                      LGPL v3
  torch, librosa, scikit-learn, ...  PyPI, see target/freeze.txt after a build

Because several of these are non-commercial or unlicensed for redistribution,
the built .app and .dmg are for personal use on the machine that built them.
Do not redistribute them. See upstream's THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.md.
